    },
    "Drop one image on the window to look at it, or two to compare them: the first is read as the baseline and the second as the candidate." : {

    },
    "Drop to process" : {

    },
    "Drop to process!" : {

    },
    "Each pane has its own display mode: **Fit**, **Actual Size (1:1)**, or **Free**. In Free, scroll or pinch over the image to zoom around the pointer, drag to move it, or use the **−** and **+** buttons and type a factor between them; the target button centres the image at 1.0 again. **View ▸ Image Size**, **Zoom In** (⌘=), **Zoom Out** (⌘-), and **Centre and Reset Zoom** do the same for every pane at once." : {

    },
    "Every action that writes a snapshot — Accept, Reject, Keep, Accept All, Discard, and Move to Trash — can be taken back with **Edit ▸ Undo** (⌘Z) and repeated with **Redo** (⇧⌘Z), until you open another project or quit." : {

    },
    "Every modified snapshot goes back to the committed version. Changes that were never committed can be put back with Edit ▸ Undo until you open another project or quit. Untracked snapshots are left alone." : {

    },
    "Every pixel is byte for byte the same." : {

    },
    "Exact" : {

    },
