    "Test source missing" : {

    },
    "The **candidate** is the image your test just recorded: the file on disk. The **baseline** is what it is measured against — the version committed to git, or a reference image you opened beside it. The baseline is always on the left and the candidate on the right." : {

    },
    "The **×** in a pane's header (or **Snapshot ▸ Close Baseline** and **Close Candidate**) closes that side and leaves the other on screen on its own." : {

    },
    "The URL is missing the required “%@” parameter." : {

    },
    "The bar under a comparison decides it. **Accept** copies the candidate over the baseline file. **Reject** copies the baseline over the candidate. Both overwrite a file on disk; when one is unavailable, the bar says why." : {

    },
    "The baseline on screen was read out of %@ and exists only for this comparison. The candidate is already the file on disk — commit it to make it the recorded baseline." : {

    },
    "The candidate is a copy of what the test run rendered, not a file in the project. Run the test again to replace it." : {

    },
    "The clipboard holds no snapshot path GimDiff recognises." : {

    },
    "The command-line tool hands work to the running app, or runs on its own:" : {

    },
    "The comparison could not be drawn." : {

    },
    "The downloaded images are scratch copies, so accepting, reverting, and deleting are turned off. **File ▸ Close Pull Request Review** deletes the copies and puts back the project you had open." : {

    },
    "The file does not exist at this path or could not be decoded." : {

    },
    "The gimdiff command" : {

    },
    "The images are different sizes, so no pixel lines up with another." : {

    },
    "The largest difference is ΔE %@. A tolerance at least that loose would call these images a match." : {

    },
    "The mask's **Tolerance** menu (also **View ▸ Diff Tolerance**) lets through differences nobody could see. It measures how far apart two pixels look, as a ΔE: at ΔE 2.3, about the smallest visible change, anti-aliasing and rounding stop being painted while real changes still are. Hover over the result to see the largest difference between the two images. GimDiff remembers the setting." : {

    },
    "The test results in “%@” could not be read." : {

    },
    "The toolbar's colour wells set the panel background and a matte behind the image, which makes a transparent snapshot readable. **View ▸ Panel Background** and **View ▸ Image Matte** offer the same presets." : {

    },
    "There are no test results for this project. Run its tests, then try again." : {

    },
